{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Transfer Learning & Fine-Tuning Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Load a pretrained backbone and inspect it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn as nn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from torchvision.models import resnet18, ResNet18_Weights"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "backbone = resnet18(weights=ResNet18_Weights.IMAGENET1K_V1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(backbone)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(\"classifier head:\", backbone.fc)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(\"feature dim:\", backbone.fc.in_features)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`ResNet18` has four stages (`layer1..layer4`) plus a stem and a `fc` head. Every torchvision classification backbone has an analogous structure."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Feature extraction \u2014 freeze everything, replace the head"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def make_feature_extractor(num_classes=10):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model = resnet18(weights=ResNet18_Weights.IMAGENET1K_V1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for p in model.parameters():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        p.requires_grad = False"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model.fc = nn.Linear(model.fc.in_features, num_classes)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return model"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model = make_feature_extractor(num_classes=10)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "trainable = sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters() if p.requires_grad)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "frozen = sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters() if not p.requires_grad)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"trainable: {trainable:>10,}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"frozen:    {frozen:>10,}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Only `model.fc` is trainable. The backbone is a frozen feature extractor."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Discriminative fine-tuning"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A utility that builds parameter groups with stage-specific learning rates."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def discriminative_param_groups(model, base_lr=1e-3, decay=0.3):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    stages = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        [\"conv1\", \"bn1\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        [\"layer1\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        [\"layer2\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        [\"layer3\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        [\"layer4\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        [\"fc\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    groups = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i, names in enumerate(stages):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        lr = base_lr * (decay ** (len(stages) - 1 - i))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        params = [p for n, p in model.named_parameters()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                  if any(n.startswith(k) for k in names)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if params:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            groups.append({\"params\": params, \"lr\": lr, \"name\": \"_\".join(names)})"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return groups"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model = resnet18(weights=ResNet18_Weights.IMAGENET1K_V1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model.fc = nn.Linear(model.fc.in_features, 10)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for p in model.parameters():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    p.requires_grad = True"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "groups = discriminative_param_groups(model)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for g in groups:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"{g['name']:>10s}  lr={g['lr']:.2e}  params={sum(p.numel() for p in g['params']):>8,}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`decay=0.3` means each stage trains at 30% of the rate of the next one. `fc` gets `base_lr`, `layer4` gets `0.3 * base_lr`, `conv1` gets `0.3^5 * base_lr \u2248 0.00243 * base_lr`. Extreme sounding; empirically it works."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: BatchNorm handling"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Helper to freeze BN running statistics without freezing its weights."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def freeze_bn_stats(model):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for m in model.modules():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if isinstance(m, (nn.BatchNorm1d, nn.BatchNorm2d, nn.BatchNorm3d)):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            m.eval()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for p in m.parameters():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                p.requires_grad = False"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return model"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Call it after you set `model.train()` at the start of every epoch. `model.train()` flips everything to training mode; this reverses it only for BN layers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: A minimal end-to-end fine-tuning loop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from torch.optim import SGD"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from torch.utils.data import DataLoader"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from torch.optim.lr_scheduler import CosineAnnealingLR"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn.functional as F"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def fine_tune(model, train_loader, val_loader, device, epochs=5, base_lr=1e-3, freeze_bn=False):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model = model.to(device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    groups = discriminative_param_groups(model, base_lr=base_lr)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    optimizer = SGD(groups, momentum=0.9, weight_decay=1e-4, nesterov=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    scheduler = CosineAnnealingLR(optimizer, T_max=epochs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for epoch in range(epochs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        model.train()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if freeze_bn:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            freeze_bn_stats(model)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        tr_loss, tr_correct, tr_total = 0.0, 0, 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for x, y in train_loader:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            x, y = x.to(device), y.to(device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            logits = model(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            loss = F.cross_entropy(logits, y, label_smoothing=0.1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            optimizer.zero_grad()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            loss.backward()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            optimizer.step()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            tr_loss += loss.item() * x.size(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            tr_total += x.size(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            tr_correct += (logits.argmax(-1) == y).sum().item()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        scheduler.step()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        model.eval()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        va_total, va_correct = 0, 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        with torch.no_grad():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for x, y in val_loader:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                x, y = x.to(device), y.to(device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                pred = model(x).argmax(-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                va_total += x.size(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                va_correct += (pred == y).sum().item()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"epoch {epoch}  train {tr_loss/tr_total:.3f}/{tr_correct/tr_total:.3f}  \""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "              f\"val {va_correct/va_total:.3f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return model"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Five epochs with the above recipe on CIFAR-10 takes `ResNet18-IMAGENET1K_V1` from ~70% zero-shot linear-probe accuracy to ~93% fine-tuned accuracy. The head alone would plateau around 86% without ever touching the backbone."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: Progressive unfreezing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A schedule that unfreezes one stage per epoch from the end toward the beginning. Mitigates feature drift at the cost of some extra epochs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def progressive_unfreeze_schedule(model):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    stages = [\"layer4\", \"layer3\", \"layer2\", \"layer1\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    yielded = set()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def start():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for p in model.parameters():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            p.requires_grad = False"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for p in model.fc.parameters():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            p.requires_grad = True"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def unfreeze(epoch):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if epoch < len(stages):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            name = stages[epoch]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            yielded.add(name)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for n, p in model.named_parameters():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                if n.startswith(name):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    p.requires_grad = True"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return name"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return start, unfreeze"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Call `start()` once before the first epoch. Call `unfreeze(epoch)` at the start of each epoch. Rebuild the optimizer whenever the set of trainable parameters changes, otherwise the frozen params still hold cached moments that confuse it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **(Easy)** Train a `ResNet18` as a linear probe (backbone frozen) and as a full fine-tune on the same synthetic-CIFAR dataset. Report both accuracies side by side. Explain which gap tells you the features transfer well and which tells you they do not.\n2. **(Medium)** Introduce a bug on purpose: set `base_lr = 1e-1` on the backbone stage instead of the head. Show the training loss explode, then recover by applying the `discriminative_param_groups` helper. Record the LR at which each stage starts diverging.\n3. **(Hard)** Take a medical imaging dataset (e.g. CheXpert-small, PatchCamelyon, or HAM10000) and compare three regimes: (a) ImageNet-pretrained frozen backbone + linear head; (b) ImageNet-pretrained fine-tune end-to-end; (c) scratch training. Report accuracy and compute cost for each. At what dataset size does scratch training become competitive?"
      ]
    }
